From 1a8fe11a323601b3b4cd25b812b48a484ff29782 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Billy Tsai <billy_tsai@aspeedtech.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 10:58:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ocp-recovery-tool: add --i3c support

Add a --i3c flag that switches the transport from I2CTransport to the
new I3CSysfsTransport. I3C has no fixed 7-bit address the way I2C
does, so device selection works differently: an explicit
-g/--i3c-group sysfs path, -b/--bus with -p/--pid to build
"<bus>-<pid>" directly, or -b/--bus alone to auto-discover the single
matching device under /sys/bus/i3c/devices/<bus>-*/ocp_recovery
(erroring out if there's zero or more than one match, asking for -p or
-g to disambiguate).

Every existing subcommand keeps working unchanged over either
transport, since Target never sees which one it's talking to.

Signed-off-by: Billy Tsai <billy_tsai@aspeedtech.com>

Upstream-Status: Pending
